I found a material mismatch between the supporting comparisons. The five-width sweep uses the simple threshold-divided-by-quantile rule; the twenty-anchor result adds a numerical clearance step. Existing records for the same eight anchors give −0.177% with clearance, versus the reported −0.303% without it, and different target-attainment counts. The negative sign survives there, but the reports do not yet describe one identical successor implementation.

