+The coherent convention is to spend power sufficient for a nominal operating point, then choose a more robust, usually slower mode under a conservative channel view. For that defense to hold, the nominal target must be a control setpoint rather than promised delivery; the lower selected mode must actually be transmitted; failed attempts must still incur energy and interference; partial delivery and conservative rejection must be permitted; and neither guaranteed 50 Mbit/s nor 90% network availability may be claimed. Those conditions substantially match the declarations and implementation. [v1.7 §1](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-probe-ws/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.7-ERRATUM-2026-09-09.md:5) had already withdrawn the availability rationale and named a prespecified tenth-percentile scoring convention.
